{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-161551",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "For a type II region $R$ with projection $D$ onto the $yz$-plane, the triple integral of a continuous function $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(y,z)}^{{u}_{2}(y,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe consider the region $R$ as a type II region enclosed between the back surface $x={u}_{1}(y,z)=1$ and the front surface $x={u}_{2}(y,z)=2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14231356/assets/e5779dc92c875bef280425ed24a17cfb53f9f2a9736292a92ccdb988044237a6.png)\n\nSo, the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,1\\le x\\le 2\\}.\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ as a type I *plane* region in the $yz$-plane with the upper curve\n\n$$\nz=1-{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14231356/assets/00f2847a8e4c927a1c6631f4aef03c57b9d28f18341b268182501ada07225382.png)\n\nHence, $D=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le 1-{y}^{2}\\}.$\n\nTherefore, we write the triple integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}V & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{y}^{2}}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{y}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡z[x]_{x=1}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{y}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
